/target
*.wasm
.DS_Store
oracle-prices-ui/.next
oracle-prices-ui/out
*.tsbuildinfo

# Lock files ARE committed here, overriding any global ignore.
#
# The scheduler image builds with `cargo build --locked`, so an untracked lock file means the
# build depends on whatever stale copy happens to sit on the host — which is exactly how a
# dependency change turns into "the lock file needs to be updated but --locked was passed" on
# a machine that never sees the fix.
#
# The worker's lock matters for a different reason: its wasm hash is what the enclave attests.
# An unpinned dependency graph means the same source can compile to a different binary, and a
# measurement nobody can reproduce is not much of a measurement.
!Cargo.lock
!scheduler/Cargo.lock
!sources/Cargo.lock
